§1 SERVED TRUTH — the composition inverted mid-card (the honest headline)
First build shipped a ground-anchored figure at the pawn origin (z=-0.15 behind
the sheet plane). The served D=64 capture came back PIXEL-IDENTICAL to BEFORE
(hero crop |A-B| max delta 11, census px=0 while the CTRL crop moved 295 px).
Instrumenting a scratch copy (temporary console print, separate export/port —
product tree untouched; scratch later deleted) proved the web engine DID execute
setup_pawn with the body built ("VDPRINT setup_pawn warden body=true" x3, real
Chromium console) — yet nothing painted. Root cause, measured from mesh_core.tres
+ the CORE_EMBLEM comment in mission_world.gd: the main core is a 3x4x3 BoxMesh
whose rim tops out at y~2, and hero_controller pins the pawn at core_main.pos —
THE HERO STANDS INSIDE THE CORE BOX. The v1.5 sheet (top 1.5u) was ALREADY under
the rim: the shipped "~8px speck" was crest medallion + box rim, and any 0..3u
figure at the origin is swallowed by the opaque box. A second scratch experiment
(BODY_OFFSET z=5.5, same export path) then RASTERIZED ON WEB — a legged blue
figure with shadow visible on the open board — proving runtime BoxMesh/Cylinder-
Mesh renders fine in the Compatibility/WebGL2 renderer (range_ring's runtime
TorusMesh precedent holds). FINAL COMPOSITION (declared in the file header):
the figure stands BODY_OFFSET = (0,0,2.6) camera-side of the box, feet on the
ground plane, feet-to-top within the WORLD_H_HERO 3u door; the byte-pinned crest
(medallion miniature + name at the pawn origin) now reads as the figure's
backdrop banner; the main sheet stays HIDDEN (declared; its G7 eff_h=3.0 pin
stays green on the hidden node, test_hero_crest.py UNTOUCHED and green). The
offset is visual-only (a child-of-pawn position — every sim position, hero
state and the pawn node itself untouched, zero-sim-writes law kept).

